<title>CHINA: China '96 tourism income at over 240 bln yuan.</title>
<headline>China '96 tourism income at over 240 bln yuan.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's tourism revenues reached more than 240 billion yuan ($29 billion) in 1996, the Financial News said on Friday.</p>
<p>Earnings from foreign tourists were more than $10 billion, up 15 percent compared with 1995 while earnings from domestic tourism were 160 billion yuan, a rise of 16 percent, the newspaper said but did not give further details.</p>
<p>China expected to earn $10.5 billion from foreign tourists in 1997, which it has declared a Year of Tourism.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
